{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"19ed3a1e43934e87f74e7df6ee7670a99c1743562cebbdb7341327d99196740b","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira reconciler outbound flow (identity mapping + dispatch)","key_entities":["resolve_mapping(provider, external_id)","jira_account_id(local_assignee)","identity_email(local_assignee)","_assignee_resolver","_assignee_is_account_id","_update_one_apply_reporter","set_reporter(jira_key, account_id)","AcliClient.update_issue","/rest/api/3/user/search","outbound_differ.py","dispatch_one.py","acli.py","acli_rest.py","outbound_fields.py","identity.py"],"problem_keywords":["outbound assignee resolution","outbound reporter resolution","jira accountid mapping","identity provider-neutral","graceful degradation","user search bootstrap"],"propositions":["Assignee resolution must fast-path through identity mappings (opaque provider + external_id) to retrieve Jira accountId, bypassing validate_assignee_exists when a mapping is found.","When no identity mapping exists for an assignee, a transient /user/search bootstrap via email exact-match (case-insensitive) attempts accountId resolution; zero or multiple exact matches degrade to string-match fallback without failing the sync.","Reporter must be applied via dedicated set_reporter REST call with resolved accountId; when accountId resolution fails, an alert is recorded (outbound-reporter-unresolved) and reporter is skipped (not sent as raw string) while other fields still apply.","HTTP 4xx errors from set_reporter (Modify-Reporter not granted) are caught and recorded as outbound-reporter-not-permitted alerts; the sync continues and other fields are still applied (soft degradation).","_assignee_resolver returns a 3-tuple (accountId|None, authoritative, is_account_id) where is_account_id indicates whether the value came from identity mapping; this sentinel is carried through changed dict and popped before ACLI delegation to skip validation.","acli.py must not import rebar core library and receives only a bool flag (assignee_is_account_id) and resolved accountId strings; all identity/mapping resolution occurs in the reconciler flow layer (outbound_differ.py, dispatch_one.py)."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785818599855942676,"uuid":"b0fa5148-75ca-46ba-ad19-0b5265e769bc"}